+# Changelog
+
+All notable changes to tally are documented here.
+
+The format follows [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/).
+tally uses [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).
+
+## [Unreleased]
+
+### Added
+
+- **`budget` subcommand** — `tally budget --month YYYY-MM` prints a per-category
+  spending-vs-budget table for any month. Each row shows how much was spent, the
+  configured monthly budget (in USD), and a status of `ok`, `warn` (≥ 80 % of
+  budget), or `over` (exceeds budget).
+- **`CATEGORY_BUDGETS`** in `tally/config.py` — monthly USD budget limits for
+  every known category (`food`, `transport`, `rent`, `entertainment`, `other`).
+- **`BUDGET_WARN_RATIO`** in `tally/config.py` — the fraction of a category
+  budget at which the budget report begins showing a `warn` state (default 0.8).
+- **`budget_status()`** in `tally/report.py` — computes per-category spend ratios
+  and states for a given month; used by the `budget` subcommand.
+
+## [2.0.0] — 2026-07-06
+
+Initial release of tally as a Python CLI package.
+
+### Added
+
+- `add` subcommand to record an expense with optional currency, date, and note.
+- `report` subcommand for month/category totals in USD.
+- `list` subcommand to show individual expense rows.
+- `export` subcommand to write all expenses as CSV.
+- `stats` subcommand for overall summary statistics (count, total, average, date span).
+- Single-file JSON store with schema versioning and forward migration.
+- Currency conversion at write time via `tally/rates.py`; all stored amounts and
+  reports are denominated in USD.
+- Five built-in categories: `food`, `transport`, `rent`, `entertainment`, `other`.
